        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "88e64d4f-9b61-3f34-969f-95ad1e59b831",
                "word": "ataraxie",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "0bf0cf78-58f9-435c-bdfa-2287ccc3be65",
                        "entry_id": "88e64d4f-9b61-3f34-969f-95ad1e59b831",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "ataraxies"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ee108fb3-bd6d-3373-9a14-b8f6de13d4ad",
                        "entry_id": "88e64d4f-9b61-3f34-969f-95ad1e59b831",
                        "glosses": [
                            "État du sage affranchi de toute émotion, de toute passion, ou bien sans troubles de l’âme."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Philosophie ancienne"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f4a4494f-c8b9-4d60-9596-aa2a9ae3e68a",
                                "sense_id": "ee108fb3-bd6d-3373-9a14-b8f6de13d4ad",
                                "text": "Tout d’abord, il ne faut pas penser que la connaissance des réalités célestes, qu’on les examine en relation à autre chose, ou pour elles-mêmes, ait une autre fin que l’ataraxie et la certitude ferme, ainsi qu’il en est pour tout le reste."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fbf97613-a18c-302f-beae-a077f7a2cbd6",
                        "entry_id": "88e64d4f-9b61-3f34-969f-95ad1e59b831",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Absence de trouble dans l’appareil digestif."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2bffcb09-3765-358a-b2de-2cf700bd005e",
                        "entry_id": "88e64d4f-9b61-3f34-969f-95ad1e59b831",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Calme de l’esprit ; état d’une personne qui ne se laisse troubler par rien ; état d’indifférence émotionnelle."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "psychiatrie & psychologie"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "15dbdd69-6886-4fba-b700-6c5264f6c390",
                                "sense_id": "2bffcb09-3765-358a-b2de-2cf700bd005e",
                                "text": "Elle prenait le visage sournois de l’ataraxie."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9b678b49-1be3-46cf-8e22-1dcc75eebdec",
                        "source_entry_id": "88e64d4f-9b61-3f34-969f-95ad1e59b831",
                        "target_lang_word": "ataraxy",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "ataraxy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a144d542-33b1-30e1-a2bd-acd28f2db04d",
                                        "entry_id": "5cd06b98-075a-3e8c-950e-3d4bfb724978",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Ataraxia; freedom from mental disturbance; imperturbability, dogged indifference."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c9747ecf-a2b2-4aa1-8a01-25ac347441fd",
                                                "sense_id": "a144d542-33b1-30e1-a2bd-acd28f2db04d",
                                                "text": "When the Pyrrhonians say, that ataraxy is the chiefe felicitie, which is the immobilitie of judgement, their meaning is not to speake it affirmatively[…]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1062844b-9948-45ca-95a4-950880285562",
                                                "sense_id": "a144d542-33b1-30e1-a2bd-acd28f2db04d",
                                                "text": "Youth all around prancing, vociferating, mocking; callow and alien youth, having to be looked after and studied and taught, as though nothing but it mattered, term after term—and now, all of a sudden, in mid-term, peace, ataraxy, a profound and leisured stillness."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "78a804c7-6a03-4fb6-bc20-1a761ee880cd",
                                                "sense_id": "a144d542-33b1-30e1-a2bd-acd28f2db04d",
                                                "text": "There was no longer any need for fortitude: he felt nothing at present and there was no point in artificial ataraxy."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8abb3f7e-e5fd-4d66-8d2c-07f8ac3fd4c4",
                                                "sense_id": "a144d542-33b1-30e1-a2bd-acd28f2db04d",
                                                "text": "I was nonplussed, I stared at my teacher, never before had his swollen face seemed so replete with indifference, stone ataraxy."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4ba3dd39-fe17-3d66-9e9c-db8806190f3d",
                                        "entry_id": "5cd06b98-075a-3e8c-950e-3d4bfb724978",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "State of psychological calm and tranquility, absence of discomfort, or metabolical inactivity."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5bd70d53-d206-4155-a159-5318dc799d35",
                                                "sense_id": "4ba3dd39-fe17-3d66-9e9c-db8806190f3d",
                                                "text": "Ataraxy can be produced by ataractics, drugs that have a calming or quieting effect."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a14d546a-e0da-4060-be50-83dad0d1a2a0",
                        "source_entry_id": "88e64d4f-9b61-3f34-969f-95ad1e59b831",
                        "target_lang_word": "ataraxia",
                        "target_lang_code": "es",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "ataraxia",
                                "target_lang_code": "es",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e3c44685-7f79-315d-9b9f-f928288f56bd",
                                        "entry_id": "a8290751-b3c0-3b3c-bb1b-5c0d1954023f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Tranquilidad consistente y profunda, estado de ausencia de toda perturbación."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "24c71427-2015-411f-a274-3b8f3e723626",
                                                "sense_id": "e3c44685-7f79-315d-9b9f-f928288f56bd",
                                                "text": "«A cada paso lo volcaba un dolor profundo. Por lo mismo, también abrió los ventanales del salón en un titánico intento por atrapar un golpe de brisa pero el ahogo aumentaba, haciéndole perder el equilibrio, de modo que se confundía, y no lograba identificar los vertiginosos ángulos, se golpeaba la cabeza contra el mobiliario, tratando de agarrarse de alguna columna y, no habiendo resistido la basca, rompió péndulos de relojes y enanos de porcelana y pinturas ancestrales y miniaturas suizas hasta que el vaivén final lo arrojó en un diván de la antecámara. En un último suspiro maldijo la ataraxia y cayó desmayado entre almohadones, con sus ojos azules grandemente abiertos»."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
